    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="0656" n="398" xml:id="pg398"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.115R221</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1575. Reagan Bale Company, Austin, Texas, shipped on <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Helge</hi> from Galveston 200 bales cotton sold to Norwegian spinner direct
                    through Norwegian Minister, Washington. Cotton paid for through National City
                    Bank. The detention of shipments to neutral purchasers is plainly illegal,
                    inflicts serious damage upon American shippers and great injury to American
                    cotton industry. Present this case to Foreign Office and insist that shipment be
                    released.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
